LuaJIT-test-cleanup (https://github.com/LuaJIT/LuaJIT-test-cleanup) has no license file. Its README (vendored here as
`README`) states the terms:

  I've removed all tests of undeterminable origin or that weren't explicitly contributed with the intention of
  being part of a public test suite.

  I hereby put all Lua/LuaJIT tests and benchmarks that I wrote under the public domain. I've removed any copyright
  headers.

  -- Mike Pall

The other tests were contributed to the repository for LuaJIT's public test suite. LuaJIT itself is under the MIT
license, Copyright (C) 2005-2026 Mike Pall. The benchmarks, which the README says may bear other copyrights, are
not vendored.
